        "original_id": "6e8e5f8e-22c6-5175-93b9-14ad4689e74c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nikolaas Tinbergen, Konrad Lorenz, William Homan Thorpe, Karl von Frisch, Patrick Bateson, Robert Hinde\n- Roles: biologist, ornithologist, zoologist, ethologist\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine\n- Topics: animal behaviour, behavioural biology\n\nFacts:\n- Konrad Lorenz was born on 7 November 1903 and was an Austrian zoologist, ethologist, and ornithologist.\n- Nikolaas Tinbergen was born on 15 April 1907 and was a Dutch biologist and ornithologist.\n- William Homan Thorpe, together with Nikolaas Tinbergen, Patrick Bateson, and Robert Hinde, contributed to the growth and acceptance of behavioural biology in Great Britain.\n- In 1973, Nikolaas Tinbergen shared the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine with Karl von Frisch and Konrad Lorenz for discoveries concerning the organisation and elicitation of individual and social behaviour patterns in animals.\n- Nikolaas Tinbergen died on 21 December 1988.\n- Konrad Lorenz died on 27 February 1989.",
